  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Introducing someone",
     "texto": [
      "**Ini teman saya** means \"this is my friend\". **Dia** can mean \"he\" or \"she\": the pronoun doesn't mark gender, unlike English. **Mereka** means \"they\"."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Two kinds of \"we\"",
     "texto": [
      "**Kita** includes the listener (\"we, you and I\"); **kami** excludes them (\"we, but not you\"). English also uses \"we\" in both cases, so pay attention to who is included."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Country and origin",
     "texto": [
      "**Orang** means person; **negara**, country. **Berasal dari** means \"to come from\". **Apakah** usually marks a yes-or-no question; you can also ask one with intonation alone."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    }
   ]
